lesson: 65
title: Bundles of ten and loose ones
stars: 0
explain: A bag of 10 is one ten. Things that are not in a bag are ones.
explain: To count everything, count the tens by tens and then add the ones.
explain: 3 bags of 10 marbles and 4 loose marbles are 30 + 4 = 34 marbles.
vars: a=name t=thing b=2..9 o=2..9
answer: 10 * b + o
exercise: {a} has {b} bags of 10 {t} and {o} loose {t}. How many {t} does {a.he} have?
exercise: There are {b} boxes with 10 {t} in each and {o} more {t} on the table. How many {t} are there in all?
exercise: {a} ties {b} bundles of 10 sticks. {o} sticks are left over. How many sticks did {a.he} have?
exercise: A shop has {b} packs of ten {t} and {o} single {t}. How many {t} does the shop have?
exercise: {a} counts {b} full rows of 10 chairs and {o} chairs in a short row. How many chairs are there?
test: {o} loose {t} lie next to {b} full bags; every bag holds ten. How many {t} is that?
test: What number has {b} tens and {o} ones?
test: {a} gets {b} ten-dollar notes and {o} one-dollar coins. How many dollars does {a.he} get?
test: How many {t} are in {b} cartons of ten, plus {o} more?
exercise: {a} has {b} tens and {o} ones. What number is that?
exercise: In a classroom in Kansas, {a} has {b} towers of 10 cubes and {o} single cubes. How many cubes does {a.he} have in total?
exercise: A school in Wales orders {b} boxes of 10 pencils and {o} extra pencils. How many pencils does it order altogether?
exercise: {a} has {o} loose {t} and {b} packets with ten {t} in each. How many {t} is that altogether?
exercise: Grandma in Ohio gives {a} {b} dimes and {o} pennies. A dime is worth 10 cents and a penny 1 cent. How many cents does {a} get?
exercise: On a farm in New Zealand there are {b} egg boxes with ten eggs each and {o} more eggs. How many eggs are there in all?
exercise: {a} counts {b.words} groups of ten {t} and {o.words} more {t}. How many {t} has {a.he} counted?
exercise: A teacher in Perth has {b} full bundles of ten straws and {o} straws not in a bundle. How many straws does the teacher have?
test: Write the number made of {o} ones and {b} tens.
test: In a Dublin library, {b} shelves hold 10 books each and a trolley holds {o} more books. What is the total number of books?
test: How many {t} does {a} own if {a.he} keeps them in {b} tins of ten with {o} left outside the tins?
test: {b} times ten, plus {o}: what is the result?
test: A Canadian hockey team packs pucks in bags of 10. They fill {b} bags and have {o} pucks over. How many pucks do they have?
test: {o} single stamps and {b} sheets of ten stamps: how many stamps altogether?
exercise: {a}'s got {b} bags of ten {t} + {o} loose ones. how many all up
exercise: {b} boxes, 10 {t} in each, and {o} more lying about. total?
exercise: {a} tied {b+1} bundles of 10 sticks — no wait, {b} — and {o} left over. how many sticks
exercise: Kai reckons {b} tens and {o} ones is {b+o}. nah, whats the actual number
test: {o} loose {t} n {b} packs of 10, how many altogether
test: {b} tens, {o} ones, and my house is number 47 lol. what number do the tens n ones make
test: {a} counts {b} bags of 10 {t} then {o} extra and says {10*b}. thats wrong innit, how many really
exam: Determine the aggregate quantity of {t} comprised in {b.words} bundles of ten together with {o.words} unbundled {t}.
exam: It is given that {a} is in possession of {b} sealed packets, each containing ten {t}, in addition to {o} loose {t}. Compute the total number of {t} so possessed.
exam: State the integer composed of {b} tens and {o} units.
exam: A consignment consists of {b} cartons of ten {t} each, supplemented by {o} individual {t}. Ascertain the total number of {t} in the consignment.
exercise: When Great-Aunt Rose passed on, she left {a} {b} ten-dollar notes and {o} one-dollar coins. How many dollars did {a} get?
exercise: {a}'s nan has the odd 'senior moment', so {a} counts her pills for her: {b} strips of 10 and {o} loose pills. How many pills are there?
test: dad's 'between jobs' so we're flogging stuff. sold {b} packs of 10 {t} and {o} loose ones. how many {t} gone, don't be thick
